<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ilghazi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1122">1122</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Najm al-Din Ilghazi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ilghazi was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkmen">Turkmen</a> emir of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/artuqid-dynasty">Artuqid dynasty</a> who ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mardin">Mardin</a> and took over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a> in 1117–1118. In 1119 he destroyed the army of the Principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ager-sanguinis">Battle of Ager Sanguinis</a>. In 1121 he and his allies were defeated by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgians">Georgians</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> IV at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-didgori">Battle of Didgori</a>.</p></div>
